\title{BARCS: Beta-Binomial Analysis and Regression for CRISPR Pooled Screens}
\description{
Fits guide-level beta-binomial regression to pooled CRISPR screen counts on an arbitrary full-rank design matrix, and tests a prespecified coefficient or linear contrast against a Student t reference whose degrees of freedom come from independent sequenced libraries rather than read depth. Guide counts are modelled against unfiltered full-library totals, so a beta-binomial variance separates sequencing precision from between-library heterogeneity. Optional negative-control calibration and guide-dispersion moderation are provided, together with several explicitly labelled guide-to-gene summaries. A guide-barcode quantification step maps raw FASTQ reads against a library annotation to produce the count matrix. The two-group special case and its method are described in Jeong and others (2019) \doi{10.1101/gr.245571.118}; the overdispersed regression construction follows Baggerly and others (2004) \doi{10.1186/1471-2105-5-144}.
}
\section{Data contracts}{

Three objects travel together through every BARCS analysis, and keeping
them aligned is the whole of the user-facing discipline:
\itemize{
\item \code{counts} is a guide-by-library matrix of raw read counts.
\item \code{totals} holds the unfiltered mapped-guide total for each library. It is
the beta-binomial denominator and must \strong{not} be recomputed after guides
are filtered out of \code{counts}.
\item \code{data} has one row per library, in exactly the same order as the columns
of \code{counts}.
}
}

\section{Workflow}{

The exported functions follow the order in which an analysis meets them:
\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=barcs_quant]{barcs_quant()}} maps FASTQ reads onto a guide library and returns
\code{counts}, \code{totals}, and per-sample read totals.
\item \code{\link[=bbreg]{bbreg()}} fits the beta-binomial mean model for a single guide, and
\code{\link[=bb_contrast]{bb_contrast()}} tests a linear combination of its coefficients.
\item \code{\link[=bb_screen]{bb_screen()}} applies that fit across a whole count matrix.
\item \code{\link[=bb_calibrate_controls]{bb_calibrate_controls()}} and \code{\link[=bb_moderate_dispersion]{bb_moderate_dispersion()}} recalibrate the
guide-level tests using negative controls and a library-wide dispersion
trend.
\item The \verb{bb_gene_*()} functions provide optional, explicitly labelled
guide-to-gene summaries.
}
}

